@base = http://localhost:8090
@token = opsflow-dev-token

### Who am I
GET {{base}}/api/session
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a ticket (triage and a workflow follow)
POST {{base}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Actor: Asha (NOC)
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Payments API down for all users", "description": "502 from the gateway since 10:40", "reporter": "noc"}

### Create a ticket with a fixed priority and workflow
POST {{base}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Release search service 5.2", "priority": "P3", "workflow": "release-request"}

### Search tickets
GET {{base}}/api/tickets?q=payments&status=ACTIONED&priority=P1&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One ticket with its events
GET {{base}}/api/tickets/OPS-1001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change priority and owner
PATCH {{base}}/api/tickets/OPS-1001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"priority": "P2", "ownerTeam": "network-team"}

### Add a note
POST {{base}}/api/tickets/OPS-1001/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"text": "Paged the on-call DBA"}

### Triage again (and start a new workflow)
POST {{base}}/api/tickets/OPS-1001/retriage
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"rerun": true}

### Resolve (closes its tracker issues)
PATCH {{base}}/api/tickets/OPS-1001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "RESOLVED"}

### Reopen
PATCH {{base}}/api/tickets/OPS-1001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "REOPENED"}

### Latest audit events
GET {{base}}/api/events/recent
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### First-version endpoint, still supported
POST {{base}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "DB connection errors", "description": "db pool exhausted, errors on checkout"}
